WEBVTT

00:42.625 --> 00:45.962
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:56.639 --> 00:57.724
Hae-seok.

00:57.807 --> 01:02.228
I just double-checked the ingredient list,
and the allergen content was missing.

01:02.312 --> 01:03.563
Oh, sorry.

01:04.481 --> 01:06.608
The labeling rules change often,

01:06.691 --> 01:08.902
so you have to be extra careful
when making the list.

01:08.985 --> 01:09.819
When I checked…

01:09.903 --> 01:11.905
Oh, Chang-ho's picking on his junior.

01:11.988 --> 01:14.449
Hey, do you want me
to squeeze your mouth shut?

01:15.116 --> 01:18.369
No, wait. I shouldn't mess with your face.

01:18.953 --> 01:21.164
Right. That would be cruel.

01:24.000 --> 01:25.585
Don't be so mean.

01:25.668 --> 01:28.296
Aren't you guys hungry?
How about tofu and kimchi?

01:28.379 --> 01:29.756
-Sure!
-Yeah!

01:29.839 --> 01:31.966
I have to finish this first.

01:32.759 --> 01:35.178
Hang on. How about some makgeolli too?

01:35.261 --> 01:37.055
-I'd love that.
-Sounds great.

01:38.097 --> 01:38.932
Let's go.

01:40.350 --> 01:41.851
Come on. Let's go.

01:42.602 --> 01:43.686
Come on.

01:43.770 --> 01:44.896
There won't be any seats.

01:44.979 --> 01:46.439
If I go, there will be.

01:58.993 --> 02:02.831
Calm down. Let's talk this out.

02:10.296 --> 02:12.048
You should've at least

02:13.883 --> 02:16.136
heard Woo-su out to the end.

02:20.348 --> 02:22.308
Heard out what?

02:23.268 --> 02:26.396
His stupid rambling about responsibility
and conscience and all that?

02:37.657 --> 02:41.661
So you didn't change.
This is who you've always been.

02:43.413 --> 02:46.416
Hae-seok, without me,

02:47.208 --> 02:48.459
The Usu

02:48.960 --> 02:51.171
would've gone under
before you even joined.

02:51.254 --> 02:53.298
You guys were able
to do research comfortably,

02:53.381 --> 02:55.592
without worrying about a thing,
thanks to me.

02:55.675 --> 02:58.469
I brought in all the development funding.

02:59.470 --> 03:01.347
But that jerk Choi Woo-su…

03:02.974 --> 03:04.726
abandoned me.

03:06.102 --> 03:08.354
Do you have any idea how I felt?

03:21.784 --> 03:23.620
And I haven't told Chang-ho yet…

03:23.703 --> 03:24.537
Yes?

03:24.621 --> 03:27.373
…but I'd like you to be the team leader.

03:27.457 --> 03:29.709
What did you just say?

03:30.376 --> 03:31.377
Our new project.

03:31.461 --> 03:33.212
THE USU
NEW PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT PROPOSAL

03:33.296 --> 03:34.714
I want you to be in charge.

03:36.090 --> 03:38.509
Woo-su, the team leader
should be Chang-ho.

03:39.177 --> 03:42.180
He has much more experience than me,

03:42.263 --> 03:43.348
and he understands--

03:43.431 --> 03:44.766
You're right.

03:44.849 --> 03:50.313
Chang-ho looks at the bigger picture,
while you focus on the details.

03:50.396 --> 03:52.106
But right now,

03:52.190 --> 03:55.652
I need a researcher
who values the small factors.

03:59.197 --> 04:01.574
Chang-ho keeps insisting
we go mass-market,

04:02.242 --> 04:04.035
but honestly, it kind of bothers me.

04:05.411 --> 04:08.706
It feels like an excuse
to leave someone behind.

04:14.879 --> 04:16.381
You pathetic loser.

04:18.341 --> 04:20.176
Stop making excuses.

04:27.684 --> 04:32.397
What happened to The Usu
was all Woo-su's fault!

04:56.796 --> 04:58.339
Mechoori.

05:02.343 --> 05:04.137
What are you doing out here in the cold?

05:05.096 --> 05:06.723
Why don't we walk a bit?

05:09.726 --> 05:12.353
FINAL EPISODE

05:40.256 --> 05:41.340
Good job.

05:45.053 --> 05:47.221
I'm saying that to the both of us.

05:48.222 --> 05:50.725
I think we deserve to hear that.

05:53.061 --> 05:55.813
If there's anything you wanted to say,
you can say it now.

05:56.397 --> 05:58.649
Let's get everything off our chests
before going home.

06:02.904 --> 06:04.572
There's nothing left to get off my chest.

06:05.323 --> 06:06.949
I've said everything I needed to say.

06:10.620 --> 06:12.371
After the incident five years ago,

06:13.998 --> 06:16.042
I went to a bus terminal

06:16.834 --> 06:19.420
and just took the next bus
that was leaving.

06:23.174 --> 06:25.927
Then I got off somewhere
I didn't even know

06:27.178 --> 06:28.221
and…

06:29.931 --> 06:31.808
kept walking aimlessly.

06:34.644 --> 06:36.813
That's how I ended up in Deokpung Village.

06:40.441 --> 06:42.110
Now that I think about it,

06:43.903 --> 06:45.488
I guess Woo-su

06:47.657 --> 06:49.742
led me to Deokpung Village.

06:54.413 --> 06:55.581
I'm glad…

06:57.750 --> 06:59.794
that Woo-su was the friend…

07:03.422 --> 07:05.007
I used to know.

07:09.137 --> 07:10.513
Hey, lean on me.

07:15.560 --> 07:16.394
Come on.

07:28.614 --> 07:30.408
This is uncomfortable.

07:32.869 --> 07:34.579
Then I'll stand like this.

07:59.187 --> 08:01.981
DAM YE-JIN, JI YUN-JI

08:18.498 --> 08:22.835
The Good Morning Cream incident shook
the cosmetics industry five years ago,

08:22.919 --> 08:27.882
leaving numerous victims harmed
by the toxic ingredients in the product.

08:27.965 --> 08:31.636
The case was closed
after CEO Choi Woo-su took his own life.

08:31.719 --> 08:36.432
But today, that truth
was overturned with a confession.

08:36.516 --> 08:39.602
The home shopping host Ji Yun-ji
made a public confession

08:39.685 --> 08:42.146
-about Good Morning Cream…
-It was Ji Yun-ji?

08:42.730 --> 08:44.857
Dam Ye-jin must have been so upset.

08:44.941 --> 08:46.150
Did you know about this?

08:46.234 --> 08:48.027
-No, I had no idea.
-Gosh…

08:48.110 --> 08:49.987
She admitted
that she had kept quiet about it.

08:50.071 --> 08:55.159
What's more, CEO Son Chang-ho
obtained the list of testers

08:55.243 --> 08:58.663
for Noori Cream and bribed them

08:58.746 --> 09:01.916
into claiming false damages.

09:01.999 --> 09:05.127
After being threatened by Son Chang-ho,

09:05.211 --> 09:07.755
Ji Yun-ji eventually confessed the truth.

09:07.838 --> 09:13.803
The police have secured voice recordings
and launched an investigation.

09:16.347 --> 09:18.558
The person you are calling is unavailable…

09:30.319 --> 09:31.862
Here's your coffee.

09:35.533 --> 09:37.410
Geez, that's hot!

09:39.954 --> 09:42.373
I told you to get me hot coffee
with a cool first sip.

09:42.456 --> 09:44.542
How many times do I have to tell you?

09:44.625 --> 09:46.002
Damn it…

09:46.085 --> 09:47.211
I'm sorry, ma'am.

09:47.295 --> 09:50.548
Mr. Cha just barely managed
to get the temperature right.

09:51.465 --> 09:52.300
Geez…

09:56.178 --> 09:58.306
SON CHANG-HO

10:00.850 --> 10:01.892
Should I take care of him?

10:04.520 --> 10:06.689
Make sure it doesn't blow back on me.

10:08.608 --> 10:10.401
I'm going to finish this and go home.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.695
Wrap things up here
and book my flight back.

10:12.778 --> 10:14.363
What about Mr. Seo, ma'am?

10:15.114 --> 10:17.491
You said Mr. Cha
took my dashcam memory card, right?

10:20.369 --> 10:22.830
We should take care
of the factory manager before I go.

10:22.913 --> 10:23.914
Yes, ma'am.

10:34.675 --> 10:35.718
This is my chance

10:36.302 --> 10:38.512
to make an impression on her.

10:59.033 --> 11:00.284
Oh, gosh…

11:00.368 --> 11:02.286
Avalokiteshvara.

11:02.370 --> 11:03.829
Mr. Seo…

11:07.792 --> 11:08.918
Father.

11:09.001 --> 11:11.253
All I did was do as Ms. Michelle ordered.

11:11.337 --> 11:13.005
I did receive a lot of money,

11:13.089 --> 11:15.466
but I was on the run.
I didn't even get to buy anything.

11:15.549 --> 11:19.011
God loves you.

11:19.095 --> 11:20.846
Then will I be forgiven?

11:20.930 --> 11:26.894
If you confess your sins
at the police station, not here.

11:32.066 --> 11:32.900
Mr. Seo…

11:32.983 --> 11:34.860
You startled me,
disappearing off like that.

11:44.370 --> 11:45.454
Darn it.

11:45.538 --> 11:48.958
And so the Lord has already forgiven you.

11:49.041 --> 11:51.794
Hold hands with those beside you

11:51.877 --> 11:53.587
and pray before the Lord.

11:55.464 --> 11:57.216
Oh, Lord!

12:09.520 --> 12:11.021
JOONG-HOON AND ERIC WERE HERE

12:33.002 --> 12:34.545
It contains recordings of Ms. Michelle

12:34.628 --> 12:37.339
ordering that microbes
be added to the essence.

12:38.132 --> 12:40.050
I'll go to the police and turn myself in,

12:40.134 --> 12:42.094
so let's never cross paths again.

12:46.932 --> 12:47.933
Shall I proceed?

12:48.726 --> 12:49.935
Yes.

12:51.729 --> 12:53.022
Darn it.

13:00.154 --> 13:03.115
Gosh. Why would you eat that?

13:03.991 --> 13:07.077
Michelle Desruets, deputy CEO
of the global skincare brand L'Étoile

13:07.161 --> 13:11.499
and potential heir to the group,
has been accused of criminal acts

13:11.582 --> 13:14.835
during a power struggle
over the group's succession.

13:14.919 --> 13:19.256
Deputy CEO Michelle was found
to have bribed a factory manager

13:19.340 --> 13:23.385
and ordered microbes to be added
to the essence planned for launch in Korea

13:23.469 --> 13:26.555
in an attempt to stop Executive Director
Eric Seo's entry into the market.

13:49.537 --> 13:50.704
Happy now?

13:52.540 --> 13:53.374
Michelle.

13:55.751 --> 13:57.795
Stop pretending to be so innocent.

13:59.171 --> 14:01.006
It's all over now anyway.

14:03.384 --> 14:04.510
We…

14:06.345 --> 14:08.097
weren't like this from the start.

14:11.433 --> 14:13.143
When we first became a family,

14:14.770 --> 14:17.147
you showed me the world.

14:19.567 --> 14:23.362
You protected me from kids
who made fun of my eye color.

14:23.445 --> 14:25.030
Don't fool yourself.

14:25.906 --> 14:28.075
I've never liked you.

14:29.076 --> 14:30.953
If you felt that I did,

14:31.954 --> 14:34.206
that's only because Father
gave me a compliment

14:34.290 --> 14:35.916
whenever I took care of you.

14:37.501 --> 14:40.045
Ever since you and your mom
barged into my life,

14:40.921 --> 14:42.840
I've been miserable every single day.

14:45.259 --> 14:48.721
I even had to share
the few words I barely managed…

14:50.264 --> 14:52.224
to exchange with Father.

15:00.774 --> 15:02.318
I just…

15:05.070 --> 15:07.531
wanted him to love me like he used to.

15:09.533 --> 15:13.662
I'll pretend I didn't hear
that you never liked me.

15:18.334 --> 15:20.669
At least in my memories,

15:22.671 --> 15:24.798
you treated me the same,

15:26.800 --> 15:28.177
whether Father was around or not.

15:52.284 --> 15:55.287
COMPLAINT

16:00.668 --> 16:02.169
L'ÉTOILE DEPUTY CEO MICHELLE

16:14.640 --> 16:16.600
I need you to do something for me.

16:30.322 --> 16:31.156
What's that?

16:37.579 --> 16:38.998
Darn it!

16:39.748 --> 16:41.750
Sir, move back!

16:42.459 --> 16:45.170
It must be your first time here.

16:45.254 --> 16:47.673
This is a one-way street.

16:47.756 --> 16:49.091
Yeah, whatever.

16:49.883 --> 16:51.301
Where's the mushroom farm?

16:53.303 --> 16:54.930
Why do you ask?

16:55.014 --> 16:57.182
If you don't know, then get lost!

16:57.933 --> 16:59.059
Move!

16:59.143 --> 17:00.477
We're busy, you punk!

17:07.901 --> 17:09.319
Geez.

17:10.654 --> 17:11.655
What?

17:28.964 --> 17:30.257
No…

17:31.550 --> 17:33.093
Mechoori…

17:40.476 --> 17:42.269
You're here.

17:43.437 --> 17:45.898
Wow, are these the mushrooms?

17:48.776 --> 17:50.569
It looks so strange.

17:50.652 --> 17:51.570
Who are you?

17:51.653 --> 17:52.988
You don't need to know.

17:53.072 --> 17:56.784
If you just get lost,
I won't hurt your pretty face.

17:57.451 --> 17:58.786
If things don't go his way,

17:58.869 --> 18:01.163
he'll resort to anything, even violence.

18:10.380 --> 18:11.381
Get out.

18:12.674 --> 18:13.967
Get out?

18:14.051 --> 18:15.844
We just have to get rid of this.

18:15.928 --> 18:17.012
Move!

18:17.721 --> 18:19.223
Don't stand around. Finish up in ten.

18:19.306 --> 18:20.766
-Yes, boss.
-Yes, boss.

18:25.604 --> 18:27.356
No… Stop!

18:37.116 --> 18:39.368
Hey, what's with you?

18:39.451 --> 18:41.328
-Don't strain yourself.
-Hey!

18:51.547 --> 18:52.381
Who are you?

18:52.464 --> 18:54.758
If you touch a single hair on him,

18:56.760 --> 18:58.053
you're all dead.

18:59.012 --> 19:00.264
Mu-won!

19:02.975 --> 19:04.101
Mr. Kang!

19:11.316 --> 19:12.151
Get him!

19:16.113 --> 19:18.407
Please pick up.

19:25.330 --> 19:27.416
-What is this?
-What the hell?

19:34.882 --> 19:38.844
You shouldn't play dirty like that.

19:45.684 --> 19:46.935
Mr. Park.

19:47.019 --> 19:50.689
Mechoori, leave the rest to us.

19:50.772 --> 19:52.482
-Yeah.
-Leave it to us.

19:53.859 --> 19:54.985
Gosh…

19:57.905 --> 19:58.822
Hey, move.

19:58.906 --> 20:00.324
Move over.

20:01.658 --> 20:03.535
What kind of group is this?

20:03.619 --> 20:05.537
Hey, you're alive.

20:05.621 --> 20:07.164
Geez.

20:07.247 --> 20:11.585
Did I not tell you it's a one-way street?

20:13.420 --> 20:18.592
In Deokpung, you get punished
for not sticking to the rules.

20:18.675 --> 20:19.509
That's right.

20:19.593 --> 20:21.678
Whatever. Shut up.

20:21.762 --> 20:22.763
Hey!

20:23.847 --> 20:25.182
-Get them!
-Let's go!

20:27.893 --> 20:28.977
Come on!

20:39.154 --> 20:40.113
Where'd that woman go?

20:42.991 --> 20:44.076
Are you all right?

21:01.009 --> 21:01.843
What a lunatic.

21:04.888 --> 21:05.931
You jerk!

21:06.682 --> 21:07.683
Darn it!

21:12.396 --> 21:13.647
Stop!

21:13.730 --> 21:15.816
Stop!

21:19.069 --> 21:21.613
What happened to my voice? Hey!

21:21.697 --> 21:23.323
That hurt! What the heck?

21:28.912 --> 21:31.039
Hey! Come here, you punk.

21:38.171 --> 21:39.548
You jerk!

21:40.257 --> 21:43.093
Hey! Fall back!

21:44.970 --> 21:46.972
How dare you!

21:48.974 --> 21:52.227
Everyone, get up.

21:52.311 --> 21:56.690
That street is the way out.

21:56.773 --> 21:58.191
Understand?

21:58.275 --> 21:59.234
Go on.

21:59.318 --> 22:00.861
The roads are dark here.

22:00.944 --> 22:02.904
Hurry up and leave.

22:07.534 --> 22:10.078
We did it!

22:10.162 --> 22:13.540
-We did it!
-We did it!

22:13.623 --> 22:14.541
We did it…

22:22.883 --> 22:24.509
Hey! Be quiet.

22:25.218 --> 22:26.678
Hey, what's that bus?

22:32.559 --> 22:35.771
This is a one-way street!

22:39.733 --> 22:41.693
Where are you going?

22:41.777 --> 22:43.862
Do you want some corn?

22:43.945 --> 22:46.406
Damn it!

22:46.490 --> 22:48.075
Pull yourself together!

22:48.158 --> 22:49.367
The others should move back.

22:49.451 --> 22:50.535
Hurry up and reverse!

22:50.619 --> 22:52.287
Hey, move!

22:53.121 --> 22:55.248
Damn it…

23:04.216 --> 23:06.551
Kwang-mo, take a look at him.

23:07.636 --> 23:10.388
You'll have to keep an eye on him.

23:16.770 --> 23:18.814
I don't think I was wrong.

23:21.650 --> 23:24.569
Still, I'm sorry.

23:30.575 --> 23:33.411
I feel like I'm the one
who made you like this. I'm sorry.

23:36.748 --> 23:38.083
I'M SORRY, THIS IS ALL MY FAULT

23:56.476 --> 23:57.477
Chang-ho!

24:02.524 --> 24:03.859
Chang-ho…

24:04.818 --> 24:06.695
Why did you come here?

24:06.778 --> 24:08.572
This only makes me more miserable.

24:08.655 --> 24:09.698
Chang-ho, don't do this.

24:10.824 --> 24:12.492
Just come down. Let's talk.

24:14.077 --> 24:15.328
It's over.

24:15.412 --> 24:18.331
Chang-ho, it's okay.

24:18.957 --> 24:22.544
Everything's okay, so just come down.

24:22.627 --> 24:24.171
I understand how you feel--

24:24.254 --> 24:25.839
No, you don't.

24:27.632 --> 24:28.633
Chang-ho!

24:32.512 --> 24:33.763
Why did you do it, then?

24:34.598 --> 24:35.599
Why…

24:40.478 --> 24:41.313
Just live.

24:45.275 --> 24:46.443
You have to live.

24:49.404 --> 24:51.031
You should live and apologize,

24:52.407 --> 24:56.036
and take responsibility.

24:57.454 --> 24:58.455
Chang-ho.

24:59.789 --> 25:01.333
Let's go back together.

25:02.584 --> 25:03.585
Chang-ho…

25:05.629 --> 25:06.755
-We did it!
-We did it!

25:06.838 --> 25:08.590
-We did it!
-We did it!

25:08.673 --> 25:10.967
-Finally!
-We finally did it!

25:28.276 --> 25:29.527
Chang-ho!

25:48.171 --> 25:49.589
Mechoori…

25:51.424 --> 25:53.093
I'm sorry.

25:54.844 --> 25:56.304
Mechoori!

25:56.388 --> 25:58.932
-Who are you?
-Sorry.

25:59.516 --> 26:02.018
-Where…
-Ms. Dam?

26:02.978 --> 26:03.979
Mechoori…

26:04.646 --> 26:05.480
What--

26:07.482 --> 26:10.110
I was so scared!

26:11.861 --> 26:13.363
What is it? Did that hurt?

26:13.446 --> 26:14.614
Are you okay? I'm sorry.

26:14.698 --> 26:15.573
Fooled…

26:17.367 --> 26:18.660
Fooled you.

26:20.829 --> 26:21.913
Seriously.

26:25.375 --> 26:26.626
Cut it out.

26:26.710 --> 26:28.044
I really got hurt here.

26:28.128 --> 26:30.630
Really? Where? Let me see--

26:31.131 --> 26:32.924
Oh, gosh! I'm so sorry.

26:33.008 --> 26:35.051
Oh, no. I'm sorry. Are you okay?

26:35.135 --> 26:36.344
Sorry…

26:44.769 --> 26:46.104
Mr. Kang.

26:50.817 --> 26:52.193
Ms. Moon.

26:54.112 --> 26:55.113
Are you all right?

26:55.196 --> 26:57.490
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

26:59.492 --> 27:00.327
Ms. Moon.

27:01.870 --> 27:03.121
My dear Ae-ra…

27:17.552 --> 27:18.720
Ae-ra,

27:19.429 --> 27:21.056
you're really strong.

27:22.349 --> 27:24.351
Should we take him to a bigger hospital?

27:25.018 --> 27:26.811
There's nothing else I can do.

27:27.604 --> 27:28.480
Right.

27:34.319 --> 27:36.363
Oh, gosh.

27:38.698 --> 27:39.949
Mechoori! You're here!

27:49.376 --> 27:50.710
What are you all doing here?

27:50.794 --> 27:53.880
We have to fix this place up
for you to make that cream.

27:53.963 --> 27:56.883
-That's right.
-These are precious mushrooms.

27:56.966 --> 27:59.928
Yeah, they're our village treasures.

28:00.011 --> 28:04.015
Of course. Let's all do our best
and clean this up.

28:04.099 --> 28:07.268
Come over after you're done.

28:07.352 --> 28:09.312
I'll boil some meat for everyone.

28:09.396 --> 28:11.022
Let's have makgeolli with it.

28:11.106 --> 28:12.440
Now we're talking!

28:19.114 --> 28:23.618
Mr. Son Chang-ho, do you admit
that you hired thugs

28:23.701 --> 28:27.705
to break into the mushroom farm
and damage the facilities?

28:28.957 --> 28:29.958
Yes.

28:35.588 --> 28:36.423
Woo-su.

28:36.506 --> 28:37.966
THE LATE CHOI WOO-SU

28:38.049 --> 28:39.509
I'm here.

28:40.718 --> 28:42.220
I'm sorry…

28:43.471 --> 28:44.472
I took so long.

28:48.393 --> 28:49.394
Woo-su.

28:51.563 --> 28:52.939
We're going to succeed this time,

28:53.481 --> 28:54.816
for all of us.

28:55.984 --> 28:57.235
So watch over us.

29:15.003 --> 29:15.879
HIT HOMESHOPPING

29:15.962 --> 29:19.424
We're doing the Noori Cream broadcast
as planned, in two weeks.

29:21.134 --> 29:21.968
So do your best.

29:22.594 --> 29:24.387
All right. Thank you.

29:26.181 --> 29:30.268
Do you know that the Good Morning Cream
incident broke out

29:30.351 --> 29:31.936
as soon as I was appointed director?

29:33.146 --> 29:36.649
And my first decision as the director
was to ignore the executives

29:37.233 --> 29:39.986
who wanted you dismissed.

29:41.613 --> 29:48.495
That means you, Dam Ye-jin,
are Dong Hyun-ki's HIT.

29:48.578 --> 29:51.414
This isn't encouragement. It's pressure.

29:56.002 --> 29:59.464
So, did you and your mother make up?

30:00.381 --> 30:01.549
What?

30:05.261 --> 30:07.972
Song Myeong-hwa's the only one
who could've convinced Ji Yun-ji.

30:11.726 --> 30:13.728
She must have mentioned you.

30:13.812 --> 30:16.439
Yun-ji has a daughter too.

30:17.315 --> 30:19.984
Song Myeong-hwa's full of pride,

30:20.068 --> 30:21.903
but she's actually a coward.

30:21.986 --> 30:23.863
Why don't you reach out to her first?

30:47.011 --> 30:48.012
Please, sit.

30:57.647 --> 30:58.648
Ms. Ji.

30:59.941 --> 31:02.944
Why are you giving this to me?

31:03.027 --> 31:06.239
Ask your mother.

31:08.032 --> 31:11.995
I heard Noori Cream was confirmed
for your broadcast.

31:15.039 --> 31:16.249
Why did you ask to see me?

31:18.251 --> 31:20.211
I wanted to ask you a favor.

31:26.426 --> 31:27.260
What?

31:27.343 --> 31:28.928
Let's do the Noori Cream launch

31:29.012 --> 31:30.930
at the mushroom farm.

31:31.514 --> 31:34.225
But then we'll have to pull
the staff out for an entire day.

31:34.309 --> 31:35.268
Would that be possible?

31:35.351 --> 31:37.937
Of course not.

31:38.021 --> 31:40.982
Plus, it's our first broadcast.

31:41.566 --> 31:44.193
Let's just do it safely at our studio.

31:44.277 --> 31:45.820
Please.

31:45.904 --> 31:49.073
Ms. Eom. Mr. Hwang.

31:52.702 --> 31:55.496
Why? Let's hear the reason first.

31:55.580 --> 31:57.123
You both know

31:57.206 --> 32:00.209
that there's a story behind the materials
for the Noori Cream.

32:00.960 --> 32:02.086
So?

32:02.170 --> 32:03.046
Sincerity.

32:03.713 --> 32:06.716
That farm can explain Noori Cream
without me having to say anything.

32:08.468 --> 32:09.844
Should I arrange outsourced staff?

32:09.928 --> 32:11.262
Mr. Hwang.

32:13.848 --> 32:16.851
Go to the farm tomorrow
and check the camera paths.

32:17.769 --> 32:18.895
All right.

32:19.729 --> 32:21.481
My lifespan is shortening by the day.

32:22.106 --> 32:24.859
You know I love you two, right?

32:25.443 --> 32:26.486
What are those?

32:26.569 --> 32:30.239
You're going to get even busier now,

32:30.323 --> 32:32.367
so I wanted to give you
some healthy snacks.

32:32.450 --> 32:33.993
Where were you hiding those?

32:34.077 --> 32:36.579
Goodness! How did you know I love these?

32:36.663 --> 32:38.539
These are my favorite flavors.

32:38.623 --> 32:39.666
I knew it.

32:39.749 --> 32:42.210
Ms. Eom, have this and calm down a bit.

32:42.293 --> 32:43.252
This is good.

32:43.878 --> 32:45.463
I'm letting it slide for this.

32:47.382 --> 32:48.716
Great work, guys. Cheers.

32:48.800 --> 32:50.176
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

32:57.016 --> 32:58.935
-I just realized something.
-What?

32:59.018 --> 33:01.562
The best appetizer
is an eight-hour meeting.

33:01.646 --> 33:03.564
This tastes so good. It's insane.

33:05.191 --> 33:07.276
Let me pour you a glass.

33:07.360 --> 33:09.529
I'm sorry, Sung-mi.

33:09.612 --> 33:10.655
Right.

33:10.738 --> 33:13.408
I'm sorry, Mr. Hwang.

33:14.617 --> 33:19.080
I'm just grateful
that I can have a drink with Ye-jin.

33:19.664 --> 33:20.581
I mean it.

33:20.665 --> 33:23.167
-Sung-mi.
-I can't believe it.

33:23.251 --> 33:24.460
Me too.

33:24.544 --> 33:27.547
I love drinking with you.

33:29.507 --> 33:33.386
Are you sure you can get home safely?

33:34.512 --> 33:37.223
Hey, I have someone to pick me up.

33:37.306 --> 33:38.433
Me too.

33:38.516 --> 33:39.851
He'll come running right away.

33:40.560 --> 33:41.519
Mr. Proper?

33:41.602 --> 33:42.645
Yes.

33:42.729 --> 33:44.689
Are you drunk?
There's no way he can come here.

33:44.772 --> 33:48.317
Hey, that's what I should say.
How could Mr. Park come here at this hour?

33:48.401 --> 33:50.778
My honey potato will fly over
from Deokpung

33:50.862 --> 33:52.947
-as soon as I say I miss him.
-My Mechoori

33:53.031 --> 33:55.324
is always waiting for me,
even at 3:00 a.m.

33:55.408 --> 33:57.577
-Don't be silly.
-Should we make a bet?

33:57.660 --> 33:59.037
On who comes first?

33:59.120 --> 34:00.079
Fine.

34:00.163 --> 34:01.122
And if you lose?

34:01.914 --> 34:03.124
Everything's on me.

34:04.167 --> 34:06.794
-Okay! Mr. Hwang, you join too.
-You too.

34:06.878 --> 34:08.129
But I don't have a girlfriend.

34:08.212 --> 34:09.839
Call someone you can trust.

34:09.922 --> 34:10.757
Let's do this.

34:10.840 --> 34:12.467
We have to call at the same time.

34:12.550 --> 34:13.968
She's ready. Mr. Hwang, come on.

34:14.052 --> 34:17.096
Get ready, set…

34:17.180 --> 34:18.181
-Go!
-Go!

34:20.933 --> 34:22.852
Mechoori, where are you right now?

34:22.935 --> 34:25.938
Honey potato, what are you doing?
I miss you.

34:33.529 --> 34:35.490
Owner of the car with plate 1040?

34:35.573 --> 34:37.241
Why aren't they picking up?

34:37.325 --> 34:38.659
Hey, babe.

34:39.660 --> 34:41.037
Sorry.

34:41.120 --> 34:42.830
My girlfriend's here. I'll get going.

34:42.914 --> 34:44.624
-I've been calling you nonstop.
-Right.

34:44.707 --> 34:46.292
-I'm so sorry…
-You'll be charged extra.

34:52.590 --> 34:55.134
Should we split the bill?

34:58.054 --> 34:59.680
-Shall we?
-Let's split it.

35:04.185 --> 35:06.646
Can you move that to the side
so they won't overlap?

35:07.605 --> 35:09.607
Move the table over here, please.

35:09.690 --> 35:12.235
Mr. Hwang, over there and there.

35:12.318 --> 35:14.612
-Please be careful.
-Yes, we'll make sure of it.

35:14.695 --> 35:15.863
Stay still.

35:15.947 --> 35:17.949
-Come on. Stay still.
-What are you doing?

35:18.032 --> 35:19.158
Mr. Park.

35:20.618 --> 35:21.994
Ms. Eom.

35:22.078 --> 35:23.788
Well, I…

35:23.871 --> 35:25.623
HAVE SOME SNACKS, EVERYONE

35:25.706 --> 35:27.208
We're here from Moon Cafe.

35:27.291 --> 35:28.876
Have some coffee!

35:28.960 --> 35:30.461
Have some coffee, everyone!

35:30.545 --> 35:33.089
Delicious coffee
made by an amazing barista.

35:33.172 --> 35:34.882
-Have some coffee.
-Stop it…

35:36.008 --> 35:37.343
-Here you go.
-Have some macarons.

35:37.426 --> 35:38.886
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

35:38.970 --> 35:39.804
Hello.

35:39.887 --> 35:43.474
Mr. Kang's really generous with his money.

35:44.225 --> 35:45.059
It's cool.

35:45.643 --> 35:46.477
Tomato.

35:47.061 --> 35:49.605
Did you just call another man "cool"?

35:49.689 --> 35:52.441
I just meant he's quite generous.

35:53.401 --> 35:54.652
That's all.

35:55.236 --> 35:57.238
No, not there. More to the left.

35:58.698 --> 36:00.449
Please keep supporting Moon Cafe.

36:05.454 --> 36:07.748
You did great today.

36:07.832 --> 36:08.875
Thank you for helping me.

36:08.958 --> 36:10.209
No problem.

36:13.921 --> 36:15.089
Ms. Moon,

36:16.174 --> 36:18.593
I'll go and help move
some heavy stuff over there.

36:19.552 --> 36:20.720
Sure.

36:32.023 --> 36:33.399
Hang on.

36:33.482 --> 36:34.650
I can carry it.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.694
Don't worry. Go on.

36:50.708 --> 36:51.876
Wait, be careful.

36:51.959 --> 36:53.502
We should carry it together…

36:56.464 --> 37:00.760
A man should work with his body,
not just his wallet.

37:04.013 --> 37:05.890
-Body?
-Yes.

37:07.892 --> 37:11.437
This is a body built through exercise.

37:11.520 --> 37:15.233
Are you sure? It doesn't seem like it.

37:16.817 --> 37:21.030
Mr. Park, how old are you exactly?

37:22.073 --> 37:23.449
Hey, we're the same age.

37:25.159 --> 37:26.577
What month? I'm September.

37:26.661 --> 37:28.955
I was born in March.

37:29.038 --> 37:32.250
I guess you were a little kid, Mu-won.

37:32.333 --> 37:33.167
A little kid?

37:35.544 --> 37:36.921
Let's settle this!

37:38.756 --> 37:40.841
That's just what I wanted.

37:43.010 --> 37:44.011
Ms. Ae-ra,

37:44.512 --> 37:45.638
do you want to go and watch?

37:46.347 --> 37:47.473
"Ms. Ae-ra"?

37:47.556 --> 37:48.766
I was born in 1989.

37:48.849 --> 37:49.725
I am older than you.

37:50.559 --> 37:52.395
This is going to be fun. Let's go.

38:00.736 --> 38:01.862
You're so cool!

38:01.946 --> 38:03.030
INSANE AURA, DON'T GIVE UP

38:03.948 --> 38:05.908
Relying on all your gear?

38:10.329 --> 38:11.205
Go, Kwang-mo!

38:17.461 --> 38:19.297
You're so cool!

38:31.267 --> 38:33.060
Ms. Moon!

38:40.860 --> 38:42.320
Yes!

38:42.403 --> 38:44.196
Yes!

38:47.116 --> 38:50.244
I feel like I'm the one who lost
after seeing him do that.

38:50.328 --> 38:51.912
I'm sorry I suggested this.

39:00.504 --> 39:02.506
DEOKPUNG YOUTH CENTER

39:03.549 --> 39:04.884
KWANG-MO
SUNG-MI

39:04.967 --> 39:08.054
My tomato!

39:12.058 --> 39:13.017
Where are you going?

39:13.100 --> 39:14.268
Did you see that?

39:14.352 --> 39:17.063
How about some hot cappuccino?

39:17.146 --> 39:18.856
Cappuccino?

39:18.939 --> 39:20.316
Aren't you having lunch?

39:20.399 --> 39:21.859
You peeked, didn't you?

39:21.942 --> 39:23.235
No, I didn't.

39:26.030 --> 39:30.701
DAM YE-JIN'S ONLY1
NOORI CREAM LAUNCH BROADCAST D-DAY

39:30.785 --> 39:33.120
Starting today, I'll be meeting you

39:33.204 --> 39:35.706
every Saturday at this hour
with Dam Ye-jin's Only1.

39:35.790 --> 39:37.708
I'm your host, Dam Ye-jin.

39:38.542 --> 39:40.002
You must be wondering

39:40.086 --> 39:41.670
what all this greenery is.

39:41.754 --> 39:44.548
This is the white flower
noori mushroom farm

39:44.632 --> 39:47.968
that produces the main ingredients
for the Noori Cream.

39:48.052 --> 39:52.098
To celebrate our launch for Noori Cream,
we invited a special guest,

39:52.181 --> 39:53.891
the nation's first love,

39:53.974 --> 39:56.852
Actress Song Myeong-hwa.

39:57.853 --> 40:00.439
Hello. I'm Song Myeong-hwa.

40:01.023 --> 40:05.069
Will you join the Noori Cream
launch broadcast as a guest?

40:07.238 --> 40:11.242
Our customers are already going crazy
over your appearance.

40:11.325 --> 40:14.328
"The goddess is here." "It feels
like our TV quality has improved."

40:14.412 --> 40:17.289
Seeing you in person,
I can tell that your skin is flawless.

40:17.373 --> 40:19.375
I put in a lot of effort.

40:19.458 --> 40:23.712
But my skin condition today
is all thanks to Noori Cream.

40:24.296 --> 40:26.799
It hasn't even been a week
since I started using it,

40:26.882 --> 40:29.718
but people have been asking me
about my skincare process.

40:29.802 --> 40:31.971
I only made one change.

40:32.054 --> 40:33.681
Using this Noori Cream.

40:33.764 --> 40:36.559
I've used dozens
of different creams before,

40:36.642 --> 40:40.604
but I've never used a cream
with such a soft texture.

40:40.688 --> 40:43.941
Right. One thing I'd like everyone
to experience for themselves

40:44.024 --> 40:46.152
is the texture.

40:46.235 --> 40:48.195
Everyone, if you look here,

40:48.279 --> 40:52.450
you can see how it gets absorbed
just with a few light swipes.

40:52.533 --> 40:54.368
The reason why this texture was made

40:54.452 --> 40:58.873
is because the researcher of Gojeuneok Bio
wanted to minimize irritation,

40:58.956 --> 41:01.876
even while applying the cream,
for users with sensitive skin.

41:02.460 --> 41:04.587
That's why there's no irritation at all.

41:04.670 --> 41:06.839
-It's very mild.
-That's right.

41:06.922 --> 41:10.634
But that doesn't mean it just evaporates.

41:10.718 --> 41:15.139
As soon as you apply it,
it feels light but still rich.

41:15.222 --> 41:17.099
Right? And that's because

41:17.183 --> 41:20.978
it contains the maximum amount
of this new ingredient from the mushroom

41:21.061 --> 41:23.272
that strengthens your skin barrier.

41:23.355 --> 41:26.692
If you look at the clinical results
displayed on the screen,

41:26.775 --> 41:29.695
this is the result
just after two weeks of use.

41:29.778 --> 41:32.907
I know that many of you
are concerned about your skin.

41:32.990 --> 41:35.201
Noori Cream was created
precisely for those

41:35.284 --> 41:37.703
who had trouble finding a cream

41:37.786 --> 41:41.332
they could use
without any skin irritation.

41:41.415 --> 41:44.126
The main benefit of this cream
is that it helps

41:44.210 --> 41:46.128
all skin types, no matter how sensitive.

41:46.212 --> 41:48.964
CEO Lee Hae-seok's
sincerity and dedication

41:49.048 --> 41:51.634
is contained in this cream.

41:52.301 --> 41:55.721
Human testing is just the bare minimum.

41:55.804 --> 41:57.932
What matters the most

41:58.015 --> 42:01.393
is how your skin changes
after applying this cream.

42:01.477 --> 42:05.397
That's why we're offering samples
with confidence.

42:05.481 --> 42:07.274
You can try it yourself and decide.

42:07.900 --> 42:11.612
Viewer 0827, you said you bought it
since you believed

42:11.695 --> 42:14.740
it would be safe for your child
with skin problems.

42:31.298 --> 42:35.803
Everyone, today's stock
is completely sold out.

42:43.310 --> 42:47.523
Thank you all for showing
your love and support.

42:47.606 --> 42:48.732
Thank you.

42:59.034 --> 43:00.786
-Great job.
-You did great.

43:00.869 --> 43:02.162
Good job.

43:19.597 --> 43:23.726
-Great work, everyone.
-Great job.

43:23.809 --> 43:25.436
-We did it!
-Good job!

43:39.283 --> 43:42.369
You said you had something to say.

43:44.121 --> 43:50.878
I have no idea how to start
untangling this mess.

43:54.840 --> 43:55.841
Did you…

43:56.842 --> 43:59.678
really believe that I wanted…

44:02.056 --> 44:03.265
to get revenge?

44:08.395 --> 44:09.396
Ye-jin.

44:12.399 --> 44:16.779
Back then, I was young and selfish.

44:18.781 --> 44:21.950
I didn't know what was truly important.

44:25.287 --> 44:29.166
I know I don't have the right to say this,

44:31.210 --> 44:32.961
but don't resent your father.

44:34.171 --> 44:36.465
He really did his best

44:38.008 --> 44:40.594
to stop you from getting hurt.

44:41.929 --> 44:43.639
I hurt you…

44:44.640 --> 44:46.141
and him…

44:48.686 --> 44:50.771
in so many ways.

44:55.234 --> 44:56.485
I'm…

44:58.278 --> 44:59.363
sorry.

45:26.598 --> 45:28.100
I'm sorry.

45:28.851 --> 45:29.810
I'm so sorry.

45:29.893 --> 45:31.603
I'm sorry, Ye-jin.

45:34.940 --> 45:38.735
I'm so sorry.

45:38.819 --> 45:40.070
I'm sorry.

45:46.535 --> 45:47.870
I'm so sorry.

46:37.794 --> 46:40.130
YOUR HEALTH IS THE MOST IMPORTANT
MAKE SURE TO EAT WELL

46:40.214 --> 46:43.050
YE-JIN, I DROPPED BY
DON'T SKIP YOUR MEALS

46:46.386 --> 46:49.556
TELL ME IF YOU WANT TO EAT ANYTHING

47:05.280 --> 47:07.783
SONGHYEON MARKET

47:07.866 --> 47:10.077
How did you make the time?

47:11.411 --> 47:12.746
I just…

47:12.829 --> 47:15.290
wanted to eat your cooking.

47:19.753 --> 47:23.465
Then I should show off my skills today.

47:25.425 --> 47:28.095
Sir, the one on the right looks better.

47:28.178 --> 47:30.764
-All right.
-Okay. I'll get that one.

47:31.390 --> 47:32.641
How about grilled pork neck?

47:32.724 --> 47:34.017
Sounds great.

47:34.101 --> 47:35.727
I'll get some pork neck too.

47:37.271 --> 47:38.146
Ma'am!

47:38.230 --> 47:40.107
Oh, my. Is it you, Ye-jin?

47:40.190 --> 47:41.400
How have you been?

47:41.483 --> 47:43.902
I loved the rice cakes here.

47:45.028 --> 47:46.029
Should we get one?

47:46.863 --> 47:47.698
Yes.

47:48.782 --> 47:49.783
We'll take this.

48:14.349 --> 48:15.517
Thanks.

48:24.318 --> 48:25.152
It's really good.

48:25.819 --> 48:26.653
Eat up.

48:33.702 --> 48:34.828
Dad.

48:37.331 --> 48:39.625
Why aren't you asking anything?

48:40.584 --> 48:42.085
You saw the broadcast.

48:48.300 --> 48:49.885
Because I feel bad.

48:55.641 --> 48:57.476
Don't say that.

48:58.393 --> 49:01.188
You're always saying you're sorry.

49:01.772 --> 49:02.939
I…

49:05.525 --> 49:07.069
I'm sorry about everything.

49:10.614 --> 49:11.990
I…

49:15.535 --> 49:18.288
played dumb all this time.

49:20.290 --> 49:24.044
I wanted you to feel hurt

49:25.754 --> 49:27.547
because…

49:30.258 --> 49:31.885
you hurt me first.

49:34.596 --> 49:36.932
But I shouldn't have done that.

49:38.392 --> 49:39.601
I'm sorry…

49:39.685 --> 49:40.727
Dad.

49:42.270 --> 49:44.523
No, don't say that.

49:45.190 --> 49:46.441
You don't have to apologize.

49:53.657 --> 49:54.866
But…

49:56.660 --> 49:58.036
are my side dishes salty?

49:59.371 --> 50:01.665
-What?
-Is that why you didn't eat them?

50:04.668 --> 50:08.630
No, it's just that Mechoori
prefers really bland food.

50:08.714 --> 50:10.006
Right?

50:10.090 --> 50:11.341
Yes.

50:11.425 --> 50:12.676
That's a relief.

50:12.759 --> 50:15.053
Were you worried about that all this time?

50:15.137 --> 50:16.763
Yes. I was.

50:21.268 --> 50:25.063
Today, we'll be making dumpling soup
with a rich broth

50:25.147 --> 50:27.065
made from beef bones.

50:27.149 --> 50:30.652
Has anyone here
tried making dumplings by hand?

50:31.153 --> 50:31.987
Just one?

50:32.612 --> 50:34.948
Today's class won't be easy, then.

50:51.631 --> 50:53.800
You're working quite hard.

50:57.137 --> 51:01.767
I want to make some for my daughter,

51:02.392 --> 51:04.603
but this is pretty hard.

51:06.730 --> 51:08.398
REVIEWS

51:09.357 --> 51:10.358
Are you nervous?

51:10.442 --> 51:11.943
You do it.

51:16.406 --> 51:17.616
No, you do it.

51:28.794 --> 51:29.795
Let's do it together.

51:29.878 --> 51:31.296
Click on the count of three.

51:31.880 --> 51:33.423
One, two.

51:33.507 --> 51:34.674
Three!

51:37.427 --> 51:38.804
EVERYONE, HURRY UP AND BUY THIS

51:38.887 --> 51:39.721
ONLY USING THIS NOW

51:39.805 --> 51:41.181
MY SKIN IMPROVED SO MUCH

51:41.264 --> 51:43.183
THIS IS INSANE!
WHY DIDN'T YOU MAKE THIS SOONER?

51:43.266 --> 51:44.768
THANK YOU FOR MAKING THIS

51:44.851 --> 51:46.102
KEEP MAKING PRODUCTS LIKE THIS

51:46.186 --> 51:47.312
BEST CHOICE OF MY LIFE

52:00.116 --> 52:03.328
SLEEPING PILLS

52:05.997 --> 52:07.332
As for this product,

52:07.415 --> 52:10.252
popular idols are all
using this these days.

52:10.335 --> 52:11.920
It's been going viral.

52:12.003 --> 52:13.255
Try it.

52:13.338 --> 52:14.965
Hey, the color's nice.

52:15.048 --> 52:16.550
There were a lot of options.

52:16.633 --> 52:17.759
That's right.

52:17.843 --> 52:19.135
It's really pretty.

52:19.219 --> 52:23.098
And this color is known
to be used by male idols.

52:23.682 --> 52:26.101
That's great. We need products like that.

52:34.776 --> 52:36.236
This is nice.

52:38.822 --> 52:39.948
Yes?

52:43.368 --> 52:44.327
Hey, Jin-yi.

52:44.411 --> 52:46.288
Hello!

52:47.539 --> 52:48.832
Welcome!

52:49.583 --> 52:50.876
I'm Na Jin-yi,

52:50.959 --> 52:53.420
who will be joining Dam Ye-jin's Only1
as an assistant host.

52:53.503 --> 52:54.880
Nice to meet you all.

52:55.714 --> 52:56.882
Nice to meet you, Jin-yi.

52:57.424 --> 52:58.258
Let's do this.

52:58.884 --> 52:59.718
Okay.

53:01.428 --> 53:02.888
-Babe.
-Yes?

53:02.971 --> 53:04.306
I want this one.

53:04.389 --> 53:05.599
I'll buy it for you.

53:05.682 --> 53:06.850
I love you, babe.

53:07.434 --> 53:08.518
Hey!

53:14.691 --> 53:16.985
Ae-ra…

53:17.068 --> 53:19.237
What?

53:19.321 --> 53:20.864
How dare you show your face here?

53:20.947 --> 53:22.657
Ms. Moon.

53:22.741 --> 53:24.159
Wait just a moment.

53:26.328 --> 53:27.954
Ms. Pang.

53:28.038 --> 53:30.332
It's been a while. It's me, Kang Mu-won.

53:30.415 --> 53:32.751
Oh, Mr. Kang. How are you?

53:33.335 --> 53:35.795
I'm great. Can I talk to you for a moment?

53:41.426 --> 53:43.219
Marriage fraud?

53:44.012 --> 53:45.305
Are you sure?

53:45.388 --> 53:47.599
No, that's not true!

53:47.682 --> 53:49.351
Who are you?

53:50.393 --> 53:52.020
Losers like you

53:53.313 --> 53:55.815
would never know how valuable
Ms. Moon's affection is.

53:55.899 --> 53:58.735
It's worth much more
than your clothes and accessories.

54:01.112 --> 54:03.949
Hey! Take off everything I gave you.

54:04.032 --> 54:05.283
No, wait…

54:06.826 --> 54:08.328
Stop that! You old woman!

54:08.411 --> 54:10.246
Old woman? You jerk!

54:11.373 --> 54:12.457
You!

54:13.083 --> 54:14.334
You spineless jerk!

54:14.417 --> 54:15.585
That hurts!

54:16.836 --> 54:18.380
You're dead!

54:19.214 --> 54:20.924
Please call the cops!

54:21.007 --> 54:22.092
Cops?

54:22.175 --> 54:23.760
-Call the cops!
-No, wait! Don't!

54:23.843 --> 54:25.595
Is that really Park Kwang-mo?

54:27.430 --> 54:29.140
He looks more handsome in person.

54:30.058 --> 54:31.601
Should I go and say hi?

54:32.394 --> 54:33.395
Excuse me.

54:34.062 --> 54:36.314
Are you Park Kwang-mo
of "Park Kwang-mo TV"?

54:39.234 --> 54:41.653
Well, I can't say I'm not.

54:41.736 --> 54:43.822
Could we have a handshake?

54:43.905 --> 54:45.532
Of course.

54:45.615 --> 54:48.535
I'm Park Kwang-mo from Deokpung Village.

54:48.618 --> 54:51.579
-Me too.
-You must be my subscribers.

54:51.663 --> 54:53.623
We are!

54:54.666 --> 54:56.835
Hello.

54:57.877 --> 54:58.878
She seems a little off.

55:01.172 --> 55:02.590
-Bye.
-Have a nice day.

55:02.674 --> 55:03.717
Have a nice day.

55:06.386 --> 55:07.721
Wow…

55:11.641 --> 55:13.643
Should I just delete your channel?

55:18.189 --> 55:19.899
You know, it kind of bothers me

55:19.983 --> 55:21.943
now that the whole world
knows how cute you are.

55:22.027 --> 55:23.528
Come on.

55:23.611 --> 55:26.781
My cherry tomato
is the only one who looks cute to me.

55:29.534 --> 55:30.410
Close your eyes.

55:36.916 --> 55:37.917
Open them.

55:40.211 --> 55:41.463
PARK KWANG-MO TV
100,000 SUBS

55:42.630 --> 55:43.840
What is this?

55:46.384 --> 55:48.303
Park Kwang-mo.

55:48.386 --> 55:51.890
I'll help you get a Gold Play Button
within a year.

55:52.891 --> 55:53.892
So let's live together.

55:57.145 --> 55:58.146
Tomato…

56:01.483 --> 56:04.235
Then will you live in Deokpung Village?

56:04.319 --> 56:05.445
Come on!

56:06.988 --> 56:08.948
That's not the point right now.

56:33.139 --> 56:38.061
I finally made you
a birthday meal, Bong-chan.

56:39.979 --> 56:42.107
Happy birthday.

56:53.118 --> 56:54.077
Sir,

56:54.869 --> 56:58.665
another magazine meeting
has been scheduled for tomorrow evening.

56:58.748 --> 57:00.500
What? As soon as I arrive in France?

57:00.583 --> 57:01.668
Yes.

57:02.585 --> 57:03.753
It's the same here and there.

57:03.837 --> 57:06.631
Everyone's really interested
in the new CEO.

57:06.714 --> 57:08.925
I made a list of some potential questions.

57:10.593 --> 57:11.594
Where is it?

57:18.518 --> 57:19.602
Are you sad to go?

57:20.270 --> 57:21.646
No.

57:21.729 --> 57:23.898
I probably won't be back for a long time.

57:24.649 --> 57:27.360
I learned a lot of things here.

57:29.028 --> 57:30.780
We're going to be very busy now.

57:31.281 --> 57:32.157
I'm counting on you.

57:32.240 --> 57:34.659
Yes, sir.

57:42.542 --> 57:47.255
It showed excellent regenerative effects
when used with Noori Cream.

57:47.839 --> 57:49.716
But this is the first sample, right?

57:49.799 --> 57:51.801
This will sell even better than the cream.

57:51.885 --> 57:53.344
-Right?
-Yes.

57:56.764 --> 57:58.266
It's all good, but…

57:58.349 --> 57:59.309
Oh, please…

57:59.392 --> 58:01.603
Seriously. Everything's perfect.

58:02.270 --> 58:06.399
But with serums,
absorption is really important.

58:06.483 --> 58:09.527
If it doesn't absorb well,
the cream you use afterward won't sink in.

58:10.153 --> 58:16.576
The texture is very refreshing and nice,
but the absorption is a little lacking.

58:16.659 --> 58:18.203
-Ms. Dam.
-Yes?

58:18.286 --> 58:20.205
You're just impatient.

58:20.288 --> 58:21.247
Look.

58:22.665 --> 58:24.667
If you just pat it a few times,

58:25.418 --> 58:27.045
it gets absorbed.

58:27.128 --> 58:31.799
Many of our customers are in a hurry
before going to work.

58:31.883 --> 58:34.427
If you add a substance
that improves absorption,

58:34.511 --> 58:37.305
I think it'll get a much better response.
Don't you think?

58:38.932 --> 58:39.933
Look.

58:40.642 --> 58:41.809
The Noori Serum

58:41.893 --> 58:44.687
was made with fermented ingredients
to increase absorption.

58:44.771 --> 58:47.899
If we add synthetic ingredients,
it would disrupt the formula

58:47.982 --> 58:49.484
and reduce its effectiveness.

58:49.567 --> 58:52.737
Ms. Dam, are you suggesting
that we lower its effectiveness?

58:53.446 --> 58:57.450
Mr. Lee, you know that's not what I mean.

58:57.534 --> 59:00.036
Then what did you mean, Ms. Dam?

59:00.119 --> 59:02.747
-Should we stop them?
-I'm the main host, you know.

59:02.830 --> 59:06.459
-It's just a discussion.
-I'm the one communicating with customers.

59:06.543 --> 59:08.169
Just continue what you were doing.

59:08.253 --> 59:11.214
There's the saying,
"What comes around goes around."

59:11.297 --> 59:12.549
-Don't you know that?
-No.

59:12.632 --> 59:14.759
I think you mean,
"What goes around comes around."

59:15.385 --> 59:16.636
DO YOU WANT TO GO EAT MALATANG?

59:16.719 --> 59:18.763
-Don't you know Newton's third law?
-No, I don't.

59:18.846 --> 59:20.223
Absorption is key for serums.

59:20.306 --> 59:21.558
HONEY POTATO
SEE YOU SOON

59:21.641 --> 59:23.768
-Geez. You're the one who…
-What?

59:23.851 --> 59:25.311
Okay. I'm sorry.

59:25.395 --> 59:27.814
-Hey!
-"Hey"?

59:27.897 --> 59:28.856
Sorry…

59:29.399 --> 59:31.901
-Ms. Dam Ye-jin!
-Yes, Mechoori!

59:32.944 --> 59:34.779
It's Matthew Lee.

59:34.862 --> 59:35.822
LEE HAE-SEOK (MECHOORI)

59:35.905 --> 59:37.323
Geez…

59:37.407 --> 59:39.701
We should just communicate
by email from now on.

59:39.784 --> 59:42.412
You're always nitpicking
at whatever I say.

59:42.495 --> 59:45.498
I actually did a lot of research
to come up with that suggestion.

59:48.251 --> 59:49.085
Three times.

59:49.711 --> 59:50.545
What?

59:55.008 --> 59:57.093
WEEKEND RULES
IF YOU BRING UP WORK, YOU HAVE TO KISS

59:57.176 --> 59:59.721
You talked about work three times,
so you owe me three kisses.

01:00:02.890 --> 01:00:04.976
-We're in the yard.
-The yard is part of my house.

01:00:05.059 --> 01:00:07.770
-That's not fair.
-Yes, it is.

01:00:07.854 --> 01:00:09.439
Come on. Three kisses.

01:00:09.522 --> 01:00:10.398
No.

01:00:11.941 --> 01:00:14.444
Hey, that's the rule! Number three.

01:00:14.527 --> 01:00:15.862
Okay, fine.

01:00:28.583 --> 01:00:30.043
So this is how you want to play it?

01:00:30.877 --> 01:00:32.795
-Wait!
-Come here.

01:00:32.879 --> 01:00:33.713
Get over here.

01:00:34.255 --> 01:00:35.381
Wait.

01:00:35.465 --> 01:00:36.299
Okay.

01:00:46.809 --> 01:00:48.019
Hang on.

01:00:50.688 --> 01:00:54.067
I really need to get this straight.

01:00:54.150 --> 01:00:54.984
What?

01:00:59.489 --> 01:01:00.990
When did you start liking me?

01:01:03.618 --> 01:01:04.702
I'm not sure.

01:01:05.578 --> 01:01:07.080
Come on. Think.

01:01:07.163 --> 01:01:09.540
When should we say we started dating?

01:01:10.291 --> 01:01:11.417
Is that important?

01:01:15.338 --> 01:01:16.756
Hey, Mr. Lee.

01:01:17.340 --> 01:01:19.967
Tell me exactly
when you started liking me.

01:01:26.265 --> 01:01:27.809
Som-yi told me

01:01:28.685 --> 01:01:33.147
that if I start wondering
whether someone slept well and ate well,

01:01:34.232 --> 01:01:36.025
that's when I've become a fan.

01:01:38.653 --> 01:01:40.279
I guess it's when I started

01:01:40.363 --> 01:01:45.493
worrying about
whether you slept well or not.

01:01:47.620 --> 01:01:48.621
That's nice.

01:01:52.709 --> 01:01:57.255
So, were there any lines
in this book that spoke to you?

01:01:59.716 --> 01:02:01.551
Well, there was a line here

01:02:02.635 --> 01:02:04.053
that said modern science

01:02:04.137 --> 01:02:08.182
still hasn't discovered
a better stabilizer than kind words.

01:02:10.935 --> 01:02:12.603
Thank you for today.

01:02:14.856 --> 01:02:16.399
Me too.

01:02:19.193 --> 01:02:23.322
DEOKPUNG COMMUNITY CENTER

01:02:25.199 --> 01:02:26.075
See you tomorrow.

01:02:26.159 --> 01:02:27.910
Make sure to sleep under your covers.

01:02:27.994 --> 01:02:29.287
It's cold at night.

01:02:29.370 --> 01:02:31.247
SEO JIN-WON AS JEON WON-TAEK

01:02:32.039 --> 01:02:33.958
YANG HEUNG-JU AS SO JONG-IL

01:02:34.041 --> 01:02:36.377
Mother. Ma'am.

01:02:37.670 --> 01:02:39.005
You're the best.

01:02:39.088 --> 01:02:41.507
I'll be back next time.

01:02:41.591 --> 01:02:43.509
JUNG SU-JIN, LEE SAEROMI AS WIVES

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:44.844
Take care of your health.

01:02:44.927 --> 01:02:46.846
KIM JUNG-HWAN AS JEON JUNG-MUK

01:02:46.929 --> 01:02:48.973
I'll buy you dinner tomorrow.

01:02:49.056 --> 01:02:50.016
What?

01:02:50.600 --> 01:02:52.351
Let's have dinner tomorrow.

01:03:01.402 --> 01:03:03.821
YOON JAE-CHAN AS HWANG KI-HONG

01:03:05.990 --> 01:03:07.241
Look at you.

01:03:08.659 --> 01:03:10.703
Som-yi, hurry up and go to bed.

01:03:10.787 --> 01:03:11.788
I'm going.

01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:13.915
AHN SE-BIN AS NA SOM-YI

01:03:14.582 --> 01:03:17.043
KIM SEO-AN AS NA JIN-YI

01:03:17.126 --> 01:03:19.462
Mom, I'm sleepy.

01:03:19.545 --> 01:03:20.963
You're sleepy?

01:03:21.047 --> 01:03:22.715
-Mom.
-Yes?

01:03:22.799 --> 01:03:24.425
Goodnight.

01:03:24.509 --> 01:03:26.135
Goodnight, Seo-a.

01:03:26.219 --> 01:03:28.930
-I love you.
-I love you.

01:03:29.013 --> 01:03:30.765
PARK AH-IN AS JI YUN-JI

01:03:32.099 --> 01:03:35.561
Good work today.
I look forward to working with you.

01:03:35.645 --> 01:03:37.855
SHIN DONG-MI AS DIRECTOR DONG

01:03:39.482 --> 01:03:42.693
I'll do better tomorrow.

01:03:43.402 --> 01:03:45.530
You already did well today.

01:03:47.782 --> 01:03:50.326
WOO HEE-JIN AS SONG MYEONG-HWA

01:03:51.285 --> 01:03:53.830
KIM YOUNG-JAE AS DAM SEOK-GYEONG

01:04:02.839 --> 01:04:04.465
You did great today.

01:04:04.549 --> 01:04:07.510
I'll love you even more tomorrow.

01:04:07.593 --> 01:04:09.720
JO BOK-RAE AS PARK KWANG-MO

01:04:10.721 --> 01:04:12.765
PARK YE-YOUNG AS EOM SUNG-MI

01:04:13.558 --> 01:04:15.393
When will we meet each other's parents?

01:04:15.476 --> 01:04:16.602
-What?
-The coffee's great.

01:04:16.686 --> 01:04:18.479
Your cappuccino is delicious.

01:04:18.563 --> 01:04:20.314
This is really tasty.

01:04:20.398 --> 01:04:23.109
And it's decaf, so I can still sleep well.

01:04:24.527 --> 01:04:26.988
JO WOO-RI AS MOON AE-RA

01:04:28.114 --> 01:04:31.075
YOON BYUNG-HEE AS KANG MU-WON

01:04:33.953 --> 01:04:35.955
I'll meet you in my dream.

01:04:36.038 --> 01:04:38.624
GOH DOO-SHIM AS YANG SANG-GEUM

01:04:41.294 --> 01:04:43.212
I feel a bit sad having to leave.

01:04:43.296 --> 01:04:45.381
You did a great job today.

01:04:46.215 --> 01:04:48.342
KIM JOONG-DON AS CHA JOONG-HOON

01:04:48.426 --> 01:04:50.553
Then, au revoir.

01:04:51.053 --> 01:04:53.014
KIM BUM AS ERIC SEO

01:04:53.097 --> 01:04:55.725
"Matthew was no longer alone,

01:04:55.808 --> 01:04:58.853
and he lived happily with his friends."

01:04:59.854 --> 01:05:00.897
The end.

01:05:03.524 --> 01:05:05.359
Som-yi gave this to me as a gift.

01:05:06.277 --> 01:05:08.154
So he's Mechoori.

01:05:09.739 --> 01:05:11.407
It's Matthew Lee.

01:05:22.501 --> 01:05:23.878
Goodnight.

01:05:24.420 --> 01:05:27.048
Sleep well.

01:05:50.821 --> 01:05:56.327
CHAE WON-BEEN AS DAM YE-JIN
AHN HYO-SEOP AS LEE HAE-SEOK

01:06:05.628 --> 01:06:07.421
SOLD OUT ON YOU

01:06:07.505 --> 01:06:13.427
THANKS TO SPECIAL GUESTS
AHN SANG-WOO AND SEO HYUN-WOO

01:06:28.526 --> 01:06:30.069
THE VILLAINS WHO NEVER MADE THE ENDING

01:06:30.152 --> 01:06:31.445
OK JA-YEON AS MICHELLE

01:06:31.529 --> 01:06:34.448
CHAE DONG-HYUN AS SON CHANG-HO

01:06:34.532 --> 01:06:37.451
JO WAN-GI AS FACTORY MANAGER
EUN SUN-WOO AS SECRETARY SHIN

01:06:37.535 --> 01:06:38.369
SPECIAL GUESTS

01:06:38.452 --> 01:06:40.413
SEO HYUN-WOO, PARK JI-HWAN, AHN SANG-WOO

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:43.416
NOH SEONG-EUN AS BONG-CHAN
KOH SEO-HEE AS YOUNG YANG SANG-GEUM

01:06:43.499 --> 01:06:45.334
JO JIN-HYEONG AS GI-BOK
NAM GWON-A AS MS. OKPO

01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:46.460
JANG EUN-SIL AS GI-SUN

01:07:31.964 --> 01:07:33.966
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
